Using default configuration, System.Text.Json?displayProperty=fullName serializes values of type object using polymorphism. This behavior becomes less consistent if you register a custom converter for object. System.Text.Json has historically hardcoded polymorphism for root-level object values but not for nested object values. Starting with .NET 7, this behavior has changed so that custom converters never use polymorphism.

