CA1831: Use AsSpan instead of Range-based indexers for string when appropriate

 Property   Value

 Rule ID   CA1831

 Title   Use AsSpan instead of Range-based indexers for string when appropriate

 Category   Performance

 Fix is breaking or non-breaking   Non-breaking

 Enabled by default in .NET 10   As warning

 Applicable languages   C# and Visual Basic

Cause

A range-indexer is used on a string and the value is implicitly assigned to ReadOnlySpan<char>.

Rule description

This rule fires when you use a range-indexer on a string and assign it to a span type. The range indexer on a [System.Span1](xref:System.Span1) is a non-copying [System.Span1.Slice*?#System_Span_1_Slice_System_Int32_System_Int32_](xref:System.Span1.Slice*?#System_Span_1_Slice_System_Int32_System_Int32_) operation, but for the range indexer on a string, the method System.String.Substring*?#System_String_Substring_System_Int32_System_Int32_ will be used instead of [System.Span1.Slice*?#System_Span_1_Slice_System_Int32_System_Int32_](xref:System.Span1.Slice*?#System_Span_1_Slice_System_Int32_System_Int32_). This produces a copy of the requested portion of the string. This copy is usually unnecessary when it's implicitly used as a [System.ReadOnlySpan1](xref:System.ReadOnlySpan1) or [System.ReadOnlyMemory1](xref:System.ReadOnlyMemory1) value. If a copy isn't intended, use the System.MemoryExtensions.AsSpan*?#System_MemoryExtensions_AsSpan_System_String_AsSpan method to avoid the unnecessary copy. If the copy is intended, either assign it to a local variable first or add an explicit cast. The analyzer only reports when an implicit cast is used on the result of the range indexer operation.

Detects

Implicit conversion:

ReadOnlySpan<char> slice = str[a..b];

Does not detect

Explicit conversion:

ReadOnlySpan<char> slice = (ReadOnlySpan<char>)str[a..b];

How to fix violations

To fix a violation of this rule, use System.MemoryExtensions.AsSpan*?#System_MemoryExtensions_AsSpan_System_String_AsSpan instead of the System.Range-based indexer on the string to avoid creating unnecessary data copies.

    public void TestMethod(string str)
    {
        // The violation occurs
        ReadOnlySpan<char> slice = str[1..3];
        ...
    }

    public void TestMethod(string str)
    {
        // The violation fixed with AsSpan extension method
        ReadOnlySpan<char> slice = str.AsSpan()[1..3];
        ...
    }

