This rule checks whether there’s a serializable class with a pointer field or property. Members that can’t be serialized can be a pointer, such as static members or fields marked with System.NonSerializedAttribute?displayProperty=nameWithType.

How to fix violations

Don't use pointer types for members in a serializable class or don't serialize the members that are pointers.

When to suppress warnings

Don't take the risk to use pointers in serializable types.

